	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Winterspring is the frozen roof of northern {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}, a high country of snowfields, pine valleys and blue ice that lies beyond the tunnels of the {link:timbermaw-furbolgs}Timbermaw{/link}. Few lands in the world are so cold, and few are so full of old things. Elven ruins sleep under the drifts. A lake holds the shards of a stolen relic beneath its ice. Dragons of the blue flight watch from caves in the hills. Yet the snow is not quiet. The {link:winterfall-furbolgs}Winterfall{/link} furbolgs have gone mad, the owl beasts of the east have turned savage, and in the far south the air grows warm and foul where demons still linger.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} first built in these valleys. It is certain that they did so long before the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}. Highborne dwelt beside {link:lake-kel-theril}Lake Kel'Theril{/link}, and the ruins of their halls remain there still. The elves remember, too, a deed of their high priestess. By the account of the Wintersaber trainers, some four thousand years ago {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} saved the queen of the frostsabers from rampaging giants, and the great cats of Winterspring have been friends of the elves ever since. Of the wildkin the druids say only that they are creatures of {red:elune}Elune{/red}, set to guard her most sacred places, and there are such places in the hills of the east.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Winterspring belongs to no nation. The night elves keep a small village at {link:starfall-village}Starfall{/link}, and the frostsaber trainers keep to their rock in the north. The heart of the land, though, is {link:everlook}Everlook{/link}, a goblin town of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link}, where {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and {link:horde}Horde{/link} trade under the eyes of the Cartel's bruisers and ask no questions of each other. Scholars have come to the hot springs, dwarves of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} dig among the ruins, and the {link:argent-dawn}Argent Dawn{/link} keeps an envoy in the town. All of them share the same troubles. The {link:winterfall-furbolgs}Winterfall tribe{/link}, who were once gentle, have begun to drink a green firewater brewed with the taint of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}, and they attack all who come near. And in {link:darkwhisper-gorge}Darkwhisper Gorge{/link}, at the southern edge of the land and beneath the heights of {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, demons of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} still dwell, and it is said that their presence warms the springs themselves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The goblins of {link:everlook}Everlook{/link}.{/b} Traders, smiths and innkeepers of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link}, guarded by the Everlook Bruisers.
• {b}The night elves of {link:starfall-village}Starfall{/link}.{/b} A handful of elves who watch over the ruins of their ancestors.
• {b}The {link:winterfall-furbolgs}Winterfall{/link} furbolgs.{/b} Once the allies of the {link:timbermaw-furbolgs}Timbermaw{/link}, now crazed and violent under their high chief.
• {b}The Timbermaw.{/b} The last sane furbolgs of the north, who hold the tunnels between Winterspring and {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}.
• {b}The blue dragonflight.{/b} Its dragons and dragonspawn keep the caves of {link:mazthoril}Mazthoril{/link}.
• {b}Beasts of the snow.{/b} Frostsabers, shardtooth bears, chillwind chimaeras, ice thistle yetis and maddened owl beasts.
• {b}The frostmaul giants.{/b} Giants of living ice who hold the valley of {link:frostwhisper-gorge}Frostwhisper Gorge{/link}.
• {b}Demons.{/b} The {link:lady-hederine}Hederine{/link} and their mistress haunt {link:darkwhisper-gorge}Darkwhisper Gorge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Highborne.{/b} Before the {link:great-sundering}Sundering{/link}, the Highborne stole a sacred crystal and tried to drain its power beside {link:lake-kel-theril}Lake Kel'Theril{/link}. The relic shattered, and their spirits remain bound to the place.
• {b}The Frostsaber Queen.{/b} {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} saved the queen of the frostsabers from the giants, and the frostsabers joined the night elves.
• {b}The {link:third-war}Third War{/link}.{/b} The {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} came to {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}. {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link} fell in the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, yet demons still linger in {link:darkwhisper-gorge}Darkwhisper Gorge{/link}, at the northern foot of the mountain. No chronicle says when they came.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Cartel has made {link:everlook}Everlook{/link} the one warm hearth in the north, and all the troubles of the snow pass through its gates.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Snows",
			text = [=[• Guests at the inn of {link:everlook}Everlook{/link} learn quickly to take a seat well away from the stove.
• The troll witch doctor of Everlook claims that every beast holds a power she calls e'ko, and that with the right charm it can be captured.
• An old medium lives alone in the hills east of Everlook. He speaks with the dead, and some say the dead answer.
• Frost giants are said to shed shards of ice so clear that they reflect power as a mirror reflects light.]=],
		},
	},
})

